%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec4ba6a512adabf4b8a74985cb2f4d14, type: 3}
  m_Name: IaIntroDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptedDialogue
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    npcLine: "You look like someone who reads the last page first. It\u2019s a useful
      habit, here at the end. Ia Lomidze \u2014 librarian, the archive on the hill,
      east wing. I have worked there for twenty years."
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: People keep bringing me their questions. What will happen. What comes next. As if the answer is filed somewhere in my stacks.
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: Is it?
      npcResponse: "Everything is, eventually. The difficulty is finding which shelf."
      animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    - playerChoiceText: What do you tell them?
      npcResponse: "That endings are written long before anyone reads them. They never find that comforting. I don\u2019t know why."
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
  - type: 0
    npcLine: "The library is still open; I open it every morning. Two people came
      yesterday, three the day before \u2014 the numbers only go one way. I live
      alone. Books are better company. They don\u2019t ask me to look away."
    animationTrigger: TalkLookDown
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: "I have already read past this part of the story. I don\u2019t say that
      to be unsettling. My papers \u2014 December expiry. I never let them lapse.
      Even now."
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: What happens next?
      npcResponse: "To you? I wouldn\u2019t say. Some things are more useful when they arrive as a surprise."
      animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    - playerChoiceText: That's an unusual thing to say at a checkpoint.
      npcResponse: Everything unusual feels very ordinary when the plot requires it.
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
